{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-simula","type":"group","x":20,"y":40,"width":540,"height":690,"label":"Simulator Foundations"},
		{"id":"group-gymint","type":"group","x":20,"y":900,"width":540,"height":690,"label":"Gym Integration"},
		{"id":"group-valida","type":"group","x":20,"y":1760,"width":540,"height":690,"label":"Validation"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9efdb11c","type":"text","text":"## SF-01 Make simulator state fully explicit and Markovian\nMove Markov-relevant runtime variables out of hidden module internals and into the formal simulator state, including ignition short timers, mechanics controller memory, and any other variables that affect future evolution. Separate true state from pure caches.","x":80,"y":80,"width":420,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a6b5db7e","type":"text","text":"## GI-01 Implement ServoControlEnv on top of WireEDMSimulator\nCreate the first real Gymnasium task env with one public step per control interval. It should apply one action, run the simulator until the next decision boundary, and always return a valid observation and reward.","x":80,"y":940,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d1da2663","type":"text","text":"## VA-01 Register ServoControl env and add Gym tests\nRegister the first env ID, add check_env coverage, and test horizon truncation, deterministic reset behavior, valid step tuples, and wire-break termination.","x":80,"y":1800,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"994505bb","type":"text","text":"## SF-02 Extract WireEDMSimulator from WireEDMEnv\nIntroduce a non-Gym simulator object that owns config, modules, RNG, compiled stepping, and the formal simulator state. Keep it as the single source of process truth and leave Gym task semantics to higher layers.","x":80,"y":440,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"4f4e5c1f","type":"text","text":"## GI-02 Add interval summaries and first scalar observation\nExpose interval charge and other control-interval summaries through info and implement the first simple scalar observation builder for the Phase 1 servo task.","x":80,"y":1300,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f35204c4","type":"text","text":"## VA-02 Add minimal SB3 smoke example\nProvide one minimal training script that instantiates the first env, runs a short SB3 smoke training loop, and performs one evaluation rollout.","x":80,"y":2160,"width":420,"height":200,"color":"6"}
	],
